// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Vision Chain — Game reward lockdown (Firestore rules)
//
// WHY: RP is the pre-listing VCN substitute. Games currently credit RP by
// writing these collections DIRECTLY from the browser, so any signed-in user
// can mint unlimited RP from the devtools console. These rules make the three
// reward collections SERVER-ONLY (writable only by the Admin SDK / Cloud
// Functions, which bypass rules). Reads stay allowed so the wallet + daily
// leaderboard keep working.
//
// HOW TO APPLY (do NOT let me deploy a full ruleset blind — it would replace
// your existing console rules and could break the app):
//   1. Firebase Console → Firestore → Rules.
//   2. Paste the three `match` blocks below INSIDE your existing
//      `match /databases/{database}/documents { ... }` block, replacing any
//      existing rules for these same collections.
//   3. Publish.
//
// ORDER MATTERS: apply this ONLY AFTER the game clients are migrated to the
// server `game.submit` action (Games Phase 2). If you lock first, the current
// client (which writes directly) will fail to record plays/credit RP.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// RP balances — server writes only; owner may read their own.
match /user_reward_points/{email} {
  allow read: if request.auth != null
              && request.auth.token.email.lower() == email;
  allow write: if false; // Cloud Functions (Admin SDK) bypass this
}

// RP ledger — server writes only; owner may read their own entries.
match /rp_history/{entryId} {
  allow read: if request.auth != null
              && request.auth.token.email.lower() == resource.data.userId;
  allow write: if false;
}

// Daily game plays / caps / leaderboard source — server writes only.
// Reads stay open to signed-in users so the daily leaderboard works.
match /mini_game_plays/{docId} {
  allow read: if request.auth != null;
  allow write: if false;
}
